  "acuerdoCambioDeNombre": "Terms and conditions of use\nORGANIC LAW OF MANAGEMENT OF IDENTITY AND CIVIL DATA\n* Art. 78 Name change\nEveryone from 18 years of age, for your own rights,for once, You can change your proper names, alter their order, delete one when it consists of more than two or increase one when it has a single name, without more than his will before the competent authority of the General Directorate of Civil Registry, Identification and Cedulation. For this purpose, the same rules of names will be followed in the inscription.\n* Art. 36 Names in birth registration\nFor the assignment of names in the birth registration, the following rules must be observed:\n1. No more than two simple names or one compound that are considered such may be assigned in Ecuadorian general use. In the case of children of a foreign father or mother, these two names may be freely chosen.\n2. Names that constitute extravagant, ridiculous or denigrate human dignity or that express things or notions may not be assigned, unless their use as names has traditionally been enshrined.\n* Art. 89 Data update\nWhen changes have been generated in the constant data in the Single Personal Registry that are evidenced in the identity card, its owner has the obligation to update and obtain a new document within thirty days. In this case, the lack of updating and obtaining the new ID within the established period will lead to a fine equivalent to 1 per thousand of the basic unified salary of the worker in general for each day of delay, up to a maximum of a unified basic salary of the worker in general.\n",
